      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 158,
      "outputTokens": 1206,
      "costUsd": 0.010933,
      "pronunciationText": "First, the algebra. The power rule works on powers of x, so rewrite the function as powers before integrating. One over x cubed is x to the minus three. Raise the power to minus two, and divide by minus two. That's minus one over two x squared, plus C on each side of zero, since x can't be zero. x to the three on two becomes x to the five on two, divided by five on two. That's two fifths of x to the five on two, which needs x to be zero or positive. And a fraction like x cubed plus two x, all over x, splits into x squared plus two. Its primitive is x cubed over three, plus two x, plus C on each side of zero."
    },
