      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 118,
      "outputTokens": 960,
      "costUsd": 0.008699,
      "pronunciationText": "Now the bracket. Treat it like x, and guess two x plus one, cubed, over three. Check by differentiating with the chain rule: differentiate the outside, keep the inside, then multiply by the derivative of the inside, which is two. So the guess differentiates to two times the bracket squared. Watch its gradient. It traces a curve exactly twice as high as the one we want. So halve the guess. Two x plus one, cubed, over six, differentiates to exactly two x plus one, squared. Dividing by the inside's rate is the reverse chain rule."
    },
