      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 88,
      "outputTokens": 620,
      "costUsd": 0.005624,
      "pronunciationText": "This works for any bracket ay x plus b. Differentiating ay x plus b, to the n plus one, multiplies by n plus one, and by the inner rate, a. So the primitive divides by both. The integral of ay x plus b, to the n, is ay x plus b to the n plus one, over a times n plus one, plus C, for a not zero and n not minus one."
