      "outputTokens": 987,
      "costUsd": 0.008952,
      "pronunciationText": "What if the outside factor is just x? The integral of x, times x squared plus one, cubed. Here x is half of two x, so the answer is half the last one: x squared plus one, to the four, over eight. A missing number can be fixed, because a constant moves through the integral sign. But with no x outside at all, the integral of x squared plus one, cubed, can't be done this way. Two x isn't a constant, so dividing by it doesn't undo the chain rule. Check it: at x equals one, the derivative of that guess is six, not eight. Here, expand instead."
    },
